The high-spin to low-spin crossover for octahedral d6 at B = 803 cm⁻¹ and C = 3078 cm⁻¹ is at Dq ≈ 1318 cm⁻¹ (Δ = 10·Dq ≈ 13,177 cm⁻¹, so Dq/B ≈ 1.64).

I got this from the spin-crossover tool, which plots the ground-term energies of the ⁵T₂g (high-spin) and ¹A₁g (low-spin) states against Δ. The curves cross at Δ ≈ 13,177 cm⁻¹. I did not independently check the tool's energy model against the textbook d6 matrix elements, so this rests on the tool's computation.

